femto patch for epub-stream 0.1.0
Subject: zip: read a deflated entry into a buffer of exactly its size

read_file_with_scratch returned BufferTooSmall as soon as the buffer was
full while compressed bytes remained. What remains may be only the end of
the stream, which produces nothing: an empty file written with DEFLATE is
two or five bytes of it, and the end marker of a larger file can fall in
the next 8 KiB read after the one that produced its last byte. Such
entries could not be read into a buffer of the size they state, which is
the size validate_mimetype and the validator allocate.

The check is removed. Inflate consumes the end of the stream without
writing. It has no room past the size the entry states (patch 0007), so a
stream that has more output than that makes no progress there and is
refused by the existing check for that, now as SizeMismatch where with a
buffer of exactly that size it was BufferTooSmall. A buffer smaller than
the stated size is still BufferTooSmall, from the check before reading.

Upstreamable.

--- a/src/zip.rs
+++ b/src/zip.rs
@@ -654,10 +654,10 @@
                         compressed_remaining -= take;
                     }
 
-                    if written >= buf.len() && (compressed_remaining > 0 || !pending.is_empty()) {
-                        return Err(ZipError::BufferTooSmall);
-                    }
-
+                    // A full buffer is not yet an error: what is left of the
+                    // stream may be only its end marker. With output still
+                    // to come and no room for it, inflate makes no progress,
+                    // which is refused below.
                     let result = miniz_oxide::inflate::stream::inflate(
                         &mut self.inflate_state,
                         pending,
